# The K-quant kernel's decode variant: packed for the matrix unit on Xe-HPG, split by width on both

# Applied against the pinned runtime, build 2026.4.0-22849-71640275d29, on top of
# patches/0003-0021. arcint 0.4.1, lever 1 of docs/milestone-0.4.1.md (DESIGN.md
# section 7.0.2az): the fully-connected K-quant kernel of patch 0021, one-row (decode)
# variant, made cheaper where a measurement said it could be.
#
# What changes (four files of 0021, no new ones):
#   kquant_utils.cl     Beside the f32 decoders, PACKERS for the subgroup matrix multiply:
#                       every quantised integer q' below 1,024 becomes the f16 bit pattern
#                       0x6400 | q' (that is f16(1024 + q')) with a shift, a mask and an or --
#                       no convert -- and the lane's 16 values are its column of the B
#                       operand; the scale and the offset are applied to the multiply's sums,
#                       not to the values (sum x*value = dl*S - mo*X, X = the same multiply
#                       against f16 1.0; Q6_K's two scales per sub-block keep the halves
#                       apart; Q8_0's sign is a xor). The 1,024x offset costs seven bits of
#                       the f32 accumulator, measured within 2e-3 of the f32 reference.
#   fully_connected_gpu_kquant.cl   The decode variant splits a column's super-blocks over
#                       the work-group's subgroups as before, but on Xe-HPG (subgroup 8) it
#                       packs the sub-block and runs the one-row matrix multiply, and on Xe2
#                       (subgroup 16) it keeps the fused multiply-add path: a one-row
#                       multiply occupies Xe2's systolic array like an eight-row one
#                       (measured 46 cycles, three times a lane's FMAs for the same 16
#                       values), and on Xe-HPG it is cheap (measured 3x over the fused path).
#                       The split stays at super-block granularity: a sub-block-granular
#                       split serialised the loads the unrolled eight-sub-block body hoists
#                       (measured, 1.6x slower on both cards).
#   fully_connected_kernel_kquant.cpp   The decode work-group is sized by the projection's
#                       width so a launch has about 4,096 (Xe2) or 8,192 (Xe-HPG) subgroups
#                       whatever N is, within the work-group limit and the row's super-block
#                       count; a fixed split of four left a narrow projection at a fraction
#                       of the card. Both variants take the subgroup size from the
#                       architecture.
#   fully_connected_gpu_test.cpp   The tolerance carries the f16-copy term on every row
#                       count; the timing test covers the gate projection at four row counts
#                       and the value and down projections at one row.
#
# MEASURED, the plugin's timing test, one launch, ten repetitions, the network's stream
# waited on (the window's spread on the 24 GB card is about 15 % between runs of the same
# binary; the 16 GiB card's is small):
#                                            24 GB card          16 GiB card
#   gate projection  N 17,408 K 5,120, M=1   225 -> 199..230 us   509 -> 179 us
#   down projection  N 5,120 K 17,408, M=1   (not timed on 0021) 241 us  |  188 us
#   value projection N 1,024 K 5,120,  M=1   (not timed on 0021)  27 us  |   27 us
#   gate projection, M=2048 (the tiled variant, unchanged)   39.6 ms   |  78.2 ms
# Readings refuted on the way, each by one timing: prefetching the next super-block,
# a K split of eight, a two-way unroll (all worse or within 6 % on Xe2); reading the
# weights lane-contiguous (7 % on the stripped skeleton, the pattern is not the floor);
# the activations per lane through plain loads or local memory (35 us and 8 us of the
# 106 us the block reads cost on Xe2 -- the matrix-unit decode was dropped there instead).
# Served (the dense Qwen3.8-27B Q4_K_M through arcint on the 24 GB card, same protocol as
# 0021's benchmark): decode 10.0 t/s at 856 prompt tokens against 9.9 on 0021 -- the 24 GB
# card's decode launch did not move, and the served rate says so; 7.4 t/s at 71,727 against
# 8.5, a difference this patch has no mechanism for and that is recorded, not attributed.
# The 16 GiB card's gain is a launch-level measurement; no GGUF-opened model is served
# there.
#
# Correctness: the eleven cases of 0021 on both cards against the host reference, the
# refusal case, the fully-connected suite otherwise unchanged.
#
# Upstream: not yet filed.

